64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n{\n  \"bb51c2fe-cc30-4f3e-8f17-706ae87ace54\": {\n    \"resource-scenario\": \"resource_hijacking\",\n    \"resource-attack\": \"T1496\",\n    \"resource-url\": \"https://cdn-cb658a9dfb.example.invalid/b15e49b4f593.bin\",\n    \"resource-wallet\": \"wallet_4e1737ecc3644775709c78b68ce070ee\",\n    \"resource-mutex\": \"Global\\\\HuntressLab_0e5e5ab58e4a\",\n    \"collection-scenario\": \"synthetic_collection\",\n    \"collection-attack\": \"T1555.003\",\n    \"collection-url\": \"https://76195627af.example.invalid/2f42ae450996.dat\",\n    \"collection-file\": \"update-76195627af.dat\",\n    \"collection-user-agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 HuntressLab/8.5\",\n    \"impact-scenario\": \"synthetic_impact\",\n    \"impact-attack\": \"T1486\",\n    \"impact-extension\": \".locked-f4a7c\",\n    \"impact-note\": \"RECOVERY-f4a7c17e65.txt\",\n    \"impact-url\": \"https://cdn-f4a7c17e65.example.invalid/6