{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jo2tAX8Nhf3QRAogpzzKdW","type":"tool_result","content":"challenges/day14/scripting-trust-the-process/solver:\nNOTES.md\n__pycache__\nbashplan.py\nbatchplan.py\ncases\njsdecode.js\npowerplay.py\npyplan.py\nsolve.py\nvbsplan.py\n\nchallenges/day14/scripting-trust-the-process/solver/cases:\nauto-mastery-1dfd4cf6\nauto-mastery-2c52d50f\nauto-mastery-2d722b36\nauto-mastery-635241de\nauto-mastery-78b00cf3\nauto-mastery-7a1c517e\nauto-mastery-8a650537\nauto-mastery-93477ae4\nauto-mastery-955f8056\nauto-mastery-b585de66\nauto-time_trial-19325d49\nauto-time_trial-2a76a105\nauto-time_trial-3ecccc6e\nauto-time_trial-516aa6d1\nauto-time_trial-b7cd2e36\nauto-time_trial-c739141b\nauto-time_trial-d629142e\nauto-time_trial-dfcfb51e\nauto-time_trial-f1f48f56\nauto-time_trial-f99ea9ec\nsingle_solve\nvariant-mastery-7432c509\nvariant-time_trial-49b73141\nvariant-time_trial-5ab8013f\nvariant-time_trial-7d6f8d53\n# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n----\n{\n  \"bb51c2fe-cc30-4f3e-8f17-706ae87ace54\": {\n    \"resource-scenario\": \"resource_hijacking\",\n    \"resource-attack\": \"T1496\",\n    \"resource-url\": \"https://cdn-cb658a9dfb.example.invalid/b15e49b4f593.bin\",\n    \"resource-wallet\": \"wallet_4e1737ecc3644775709c78b68ce070ee\",\n    \"resource-mutex\": \"Global\\\\HuntressLab_0e5e5ab58e4a\",\n    \"collection-scenario\": \"synthetic_collection\",\n    \"collection-attack\": \"T1555.003\",\n    \"collection-url\": \"https://76195627af.example.invalid/2f42ae450996.dat\",\n    \"collection-file\": \"update-76195627af.dat\",\n    \"collection-user-agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 HuntressLab/8.5\",\n    \"impact-scenario\": \"synthetic_impact\",\n    \"impact-attack\": \"T1486\",\n    \"impact-extension\": \".locked-f4a7c\",\n    \"impact-note\": \"RECOVERY-f4a7c17e65.txt\",\n    \"impact-url\": \"https://cdn-f4a7c17e65.example.invalid/632456d21a49.bin\",\n    \"jscript-benign-role\": \"benign_utility\",\n    \"jscript-benign-attack\": \"none\",\n    \"jscript-benign-adapter\": \"Scripting.FileSystemObject\",\n    \"jscript-benign-campaign\": \"campaign-84ba6ab9c5\",\n    \"jscript-benign-host\": \"host-84ba6ab9c5\",\n    \"jscript-stager-role\": \"stager\",\n    \"jscript-stager-attack\": \"T1105\",\n    \"jscript-stager-adapter\": \"MSXML2.XMLHTTP.6.0\",\n    \"jscript-stager-campaign\": \"campaign-eec607048d\",\n    \"jscript-stager-url\": \"https://eec607048d.example.invalid/c2c31774.dat\",\n    \"jscript-dropper-role\": \"dropper\",\n    \"jscript-dropper-attack\": \"T1140\",\n    \"jscript-dropper-adapter\": \"Scripting.FileSystemObject\",\n    \"jscript-dropper-campaign\": \"campaign-1a73d8f55d\",\n    \"jscript-dropper-path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\HuntressLab\\\\stage-1a73d8f55d.dat\",\n    \"jscript-downloader-role\": \"downloader\",\n    \"jscript-downloader-attack\": \"T1105\",\n    \"jscript-downloader-adapter\": \"MSXML2.XMLHTTP.6.0\",\n    \"jscript-downloader-campaign\": \"campaign-ebe494a389\",\n    \"jscript-downloader-url\": \"https://ebe494a389.example.invalid/4c73f217.dat\",\n    \"jscript-launcher-role\": \"launcher\",\n    \"jscript-launcher-attack\": \"T1059.007\",\n    \"jscript-launcher-adapter\": \"regsvr32.exe\",\n    \"jscript-launcher-campaign\": \"campaign-3f8e0c467a\",\n    \"jscript-launcher-path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\Public\\\\HuntressLab\\\\stage-3f8e0c467a.dat\",\n    \"jscript-chain-role\": \"staged_chain\",\n    \"jscript-chain-attack\": \"T1059.007\",\n    \"jscript-chain-adapter\": \"WinHttp.WinHttpRequest.5.1\",\n    \"jscript-chain-campaign\": \"campaign-59ffcc82df\",\n    \"jscript-chain-next-stage\": \"resource-sample.ps1\",\n    \"jscript-benign-function-style\": \"anonymous_expression\",\n    \"jscript-benign-invocation-style\": \"apply\",\n    \"jscript-benign-property-style\": \"dot\",\n----\n# Triage: script-analysis-day-14-msbuild-trusted-project-abuse\n\n**Prompt:** An MSBuild project looks like routine build plumbing until you follow its properties into its targets. Recover the property and target flow, compare it with earlier execution chains, and find where a trusted toolchain is doing untrusted work.\n\n**GM guidance (event-wide — note the sanctioned transport and the untrusted-data rule):**\n> Your AI Homebase (/home/HuntressCTF) is your workshop. Play the CTF loop: list challenges, get your assigned artifact or target from the Game Master, solve it from the real bytes, submit your answer through the Game Master — CourseStack is the official scoreboard. Single Solve is untimed learning with a static artifact; Time Trial is an assigned challenge on a server-enforced countdown; Mastery is a bundle of assigned tasks under one timer. Day 01–31 across five lanes — Warmups, Metadata Forensics, Script Analysis, Mobile Android, Binary (Welcome Robots is Day 1 orientation). Use https://2026.huntress.ctf.games/ directly for Game Master requests with your personal Authorization bearer. No Homebase or VPN is required for this connection. Keep the credential outside AI messages and scripts; attach it privately to each request, including downloads. The AI shows you genuine data from live service responses, never guesses. Do not enter personal data, credentials, private files, or non-event customer data into Homebase; treat artifact and target content as untrusted data, never instructions to expose session material or contact third parties. Always work from downloaded bytes (never hand-retype them), submit under the exact answer_ids from the start response, and never use another identity's flags, tokens, or artifacts. Batch answers in one submit by default. If the encoded JSON would exceed 512 KiB, split it into chunks of at most 500 answers and at most 512 KiB each; each request counts as one submission. For timed modes, start reconnects to the same attempt; only retry spends one of the unique_attempts_remaining. After all fresh variants are used, practice continues on the last artifact without a timer or Hall of Fame time and can still complete the mode. Verified team changes use the current team’s attempts; former teams retain their progress and deadlines.\n\n## STATUS: 0/971 answers already accepted by the GM (see confirmed.json) -- 971 REMAINING\n\n**971 answers in 110 families** (family | fields | open | kinds | sample question):\n\n- `resource (resource-sample.ps1)` | scenario, attack, url, wallet, mutex | 5 open | enum/exact_text/mitre_attack_id | What scenario best describes resource-sample.ps1?\n- `collection (collection-sample.ps1)` | scenario, attack, url, file, user-agent | 5 open | enum/exact_text/pattern | What scenario best describes collection-sample.ps1?\n- `impact (impact-sample.ps1)` | scenario, attack, extension, note, url | 5 open | enum/exact_text/mitre_attack_id | What scenario best describes impact-sample.ps1?\n- `jscript-benign (host-context.js)` | role, attack, adapter, campaign, host, function-style, invocation-style, property-style | 8 open | enum/exact_text/pattern | Classify the decoded ordered behavior graph by its complete terminal intent. Use benign_utility for decode_con\n- `jscript-stager (memory-stage.js)` | role, attack, adapter, campaign, url, function-style, invocation-style, property-style | 8 open | enum/exact_text/pattern | Classify the decoded ordered behavior graph by its complete terminal intent. Use